  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "hqcWXmuRHInGyH2pq8qd7XFjYTw=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:39:25.329Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The `role-based-auth` recipe puts authorization **inside the reducer**, reading the signer off the action context. Because roles are ordinary document state, they replicate with the document \u2014 every peer enforces the same rules without a central policy service, and the rules hold no matter which editor, subgraph, or script fired the action.\n\nThe state is just address lists:\n\n```graphql\ntype RoleBasedAuthState {\n  creator: String\n  admins: [String!]!\n  members: [String!]!\n  notes: [Note!]!\n}\n```\n\nEvery operation opens with the same guard, and role-mutating operations add `requireAdmin(state, address)`:\n\n```ts\nconst address = action.context?.signer?.user?.address;\nif (!address) throw new NotAuthorized(\"User is not authenticated\");\n```\n\nThe permission model is small and worth copying: `bootstrap` may be called by anyone but only once, and it makes the caller the permanent `creator` and first admin \u2014 creator auto-promotion, with no demotion path (`revokeAdmin` throws `CannotRevokeCreator`). It also throws `LastAdmin` rather than allowing the admin set to be emptied, so the document cannot be locked out. The domain action `writeNote` is gated on member-or-higher and throws `NotAuthorized` for a caller with no role.\n\n**How rejection surfaces is the part that trips people up.** A thrown reducer error does not propagate to the caller as an exception. The framework captures it and records it as `operation.error` on the resulting document \u2014 the operation is still appended, and the state is unchanged. Callers detect rejection by inspecting the operation log, and tests must read `operations.global[n].error` rather than using `.toThrow()`.\n\nErrors are a typed taxonomy generated into `gen/access/error.ts` (`AlreadyBootstrapped`, `CannotRevokeCreator`, `LastAdmin`, `AddressAlreadyAdmin`, `NotAuthorized`), so each failure is distinguishable rather than one generic denial.\n\nNote the scope of the guarantee: this gates *writes* deterministically on every replica, but it does not hide state \u2014 anyone who can read the document reads the whole document, roles included.\n\nProvenance: academy `05-Lookup/00-Cookbook.md`, Role-Based Auth recipe, academy 6.2.2-dev.45.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T14:39:24.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:39:25.329Z"
    }
  },
